From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 04:26:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Add composite index on notifications (user_id, is_read);
 complete full-directory perf audit

Finished the thorough pass requested after the first audit only
covered the highest-traffic report/country-data paths. Went through
everything not yet checked: data_scripts/, all remaining backend
models, the rest of the Observatory component family, and the
remaining pages/admin panels.

Composite index on notifications (user_id, is_read)
(server/models/notification.py, new migration):
get_unread_count() and mark_all_read() both filter user_id AND
is_read together. get_unread_count() specifically backs the navbar's
unread-notification dot, polled every 30 seconds per signed-in user
for as long as they have a tab open - likely one of the single
highest-frequency queries in the app. user_id and is_read already
had their own single-column indexes, but EXPLAIN QUERY PLAN confirmed
a query filtering both only used the user_id index and still had to
scan every one of that user's notification rows to check is_read one
at a time. With the composite index, the same query now resolves via
a covering index seek - SQLite doesn't even need to touch the table
rows, just the index itself, to answer the COUNT(*).

Same treatment as the reports composite index from the previous
commit: declared as __table_args__ on the model AND as a migration,
verified byte-identical index sets from both
Base.metadata.create_all() and `alembic upgrade head`.

Everything else checked, nothing else changed:
- data_scripts/ (etti_extract.py, gtbi_extract.py,
  combine_country_data.py, country_profiles_extract.py,
  merge_remainder_profiles.py) - all offline, single-pass, O(1) dict
  lookups, already using openpyxl's read_only/iter_rows streaming
  mode. Small N (~200 countries) regardless.
- Remaining backend models (user.py, donation.py, enrollment.py,
  fellow.py, favorite_report.py, saved_chart.py, user_event.py,
  document.py, both password_reset_*.py) - systematically scanned
  every for-loop in every file (and in app.py) for a query call
  inside its body: zero N+1 patterns found. donation.py/enrollment.py
  filter every indexed column individually, no compound WHERE clauses
  that would benefit from a composite index.
- ChartsSection.jsx / NigeriaObservatory.jsx (the two largest
  Observatory components, 679 and 279 lines) - already memoize the
  expensive country-dataset-wide derived data with useMemo.
  ChartsSection.jsx does have some O(panels x years) nested
  filter/find calls building comparison-chart data, but `panels` is
  a small array a user builds by manually clicking "add panel" one at
  a time (no realistic path to more than a few dozen) - flagged as a
  theoretical, not practical, concern rather than "fixed" by adding
  Map-based lookups that would cost more than they'd save at this
  scale.
- SearchBar.jsx - filters a small static in-memory country list per
  keystroke, no network call involved, no debounce needed.
- ReportCategoryControl.jsx - already correctly paginated
  (fetchAllReportsAdmin with real limit/offset, page controls, total
  count) - this is what the report-list pages fixed in the previous
  commit should have looked like from the start.
- GET /api/fellows is deliberately unpaginated (returns every
  fellow, no ?limit=) - correct as-is, not a bug: fellows are a small
  curated roster meant to be shown in full, not user-generated content
  that grows unbounded like reports.

Not checked (main branch only, not on database yet): the
reviewer-role/deletion-workflow pages and their backing routes
(PeerReviewDeletions.jsx, DeletedReportsPage.jsx, GET
/api/reports/all's actual route implementation) - same caveat as the
previous commit's summary.
